  "synonym_discrimination": {
    "words": [
      "divide-v",
      "split-v",
      "separate-v"
    ],
    "note": "**Divide** is the usual word for making planned, often equal, parts (*divide the class into groups*). **Split** is less formal and often suggests breaking along a line or sharing quickly (*split the bill*). **Separate** means to move apart people or things that were together, with no idea of equal parts (*separate the white clothes from the dark ones*)."
  },
